  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Outside, thugs sent by a jealous ex-boyfriend grab Denis. Meanwhile, in the office, Chef Barinov protests that pretending to be disabled is wrong, but Mikhail Jekovich argues that Malouda's sympathy makes Viktor the secret main ingredient for winning a star.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "denis",
      "t": "Скажите, что тут за дела?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "denis",
      "t": "Смотрю, ты совсем не меняешься.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Миша, что это за шутки?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ну какой я тебе инвалид?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Ты недавно из комы вышел.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Так что я не соврал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Я только слегка всё приукрасил.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Ты ему простой чебурек пожарь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "И это будет кулинарный шедевр!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "А знаешь, почему так будет?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Ты сейчас наш главный ингредиент.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мне эта затея не нравится.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "denis",
      "t": "Скажите, что тут за дела?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Tell me, what is going on here?' Denis anchors the line on 'say', while 'things to do' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "denis",
      "t": "Смотрю, ты совсем не меняешься.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I see you do not change at all.' In Russian, the idea of 'watch' flows naturally into 'to change' without extra filler words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Миша, что это за шутки?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Misha, what kind of jokes are these?' Notice how Russian expresses 'Misha' and 'jokes' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ну какой я тебе инвалид?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Well, how am I a disabled person to you?' Notice how Russian expresses 'come on' and 'disabled person' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Ты недавно из комы вышел.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You recently came out of a coma.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'you' before landing on 'stepped out'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Так что я не соврал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'So I did not even lie.' Notice how Russian expresses 'so' and 'lied' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Я только слегка всё приукрасил.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I only embellished everything slightly.' Mikhail brings out the contrast between 'I' and 'only' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Ты ему простой чебурек пожарь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Fry him a simple cheburek.' In Russian, the idea of 'you' flows naturally into 'fry' without extra filler words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "И это будет кулинарный шедевр!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And it will be a culinary masterpiece!' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'and' and finishing on 'masterpiece'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "А знаешь, почему так будет?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And do you know why it will be like that?' Mikhail anchors the line on 'and', while 'will be' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Ты сейчас наш главный ингредиент.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Right now you are our main ingredient.' The grammar packs 'you' and 'ingredient' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мне эта затея не нравится.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I do not like this idea.' Notice how Russian expresses 'to me' and 'pleases' with crisp inflection rather than helper words. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
